title: Isosurface
manual: graphics/#c2-cube

Draws isosurfaces of a field of the system, one of its derivatives or an arithmetic
expression of the fields, as an object of the view. Tools > Field Plots > Isosurface creates
an isosurface object and opens its editor. The quantity is sampled on a grid over a region,
and any number of isosurfaces are drawn from that grid, each with its own isovalue and a
single color or a color map of another field.

# Options

- "Name" and "Show": the name of the object and whether it is drawn.
- "Property": a quantity of a field (value, gradient components, gradient norm, Hessian
  components or Laplacian) or an "Expression" of the fields, for instance "$1 - $2".
- "Region": the "Mode" of the region the grid spans (the whole cell, a box, a
  parallelepiped or, in molecules, the box bounding the atoms grown by a "Buffer (Å)"), with
  its points and a "Pick" button for each. Only the whole cell gives a periodic grid.
- "Grid": the "Level" of the grid, from coarse to very fine, the native grid of a grid field,
  or "Custom" (points along each axis or points per Å). "Calculate Grid" samples the quantity:
  the options above have no effect until it is pressed. "Estimate Cost" predicts the time.
- "Isosurfaces": a histogram of the values on the grid, whose lines can be dragged to set
  the isovalues, and a table with one row per isosurface: whether it is drawn, its "Mode" (a
  single color, or a field or expression mapped on it), its "Color/map", its "Isovalue" and
  what it "Encloses" (the fraction of the integral of |f| and of the volume). "Add" adds an
  isosurface; the close icon removes one.
- "Color map of isosurface": for a mapped isosurface, the "Colormap", "Opacity" and
  "Range" of mapped values ("Auto range" or fixed). "Add Color Bar" adds a color bar object.

# Notes

The region is shown as a box in the view while the editor is open. "Reset" restores the
defaults. The Calculate Grid window writes such grids to files.
